{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890194",
      "title": "Diving Into Generics",
      "sourceHash": "0b6104a2fa71682bf9af57d04f57ed15460064b99dccd5718ef1780fb1f1cca1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 4.99,
          "en": "Now, we'll of course, work a lot with functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.99,
          "end": 8.03,
          "en": "once we start working with React and TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.03,
          "end": 9.28,
          "en": "and therefore we'll then see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.28,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "all those function types in action there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 15.2,
          "en": "I wanna conclude this basic introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.2,
          "end": 18.56,
          "en": "to TypeScript with a slightly more advanced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.56,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "yet very important TypeScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.373,
          "en": "And that would be Generics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.57,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "Now this can be tricky to wrap your head around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "but I'll try my best to explain it such that it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 35.77,
          "en": "Let's say we have a function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.77,
          "end": 37.957,
          "en": "which I'll name 'insertAtBeginning',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.842,
          "end": 42.84,
          "en": "and this function takes an array and the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.84,
          "end": 44.86,
          "en": "as parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.86,
          "end": 46.627,
          "en": "and the array should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.627,
          "end": 49.42,
          "en": "any array full of any kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.42,
          "end": 51.82,
          "en": "And the values should be any kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.82,
          "end": 53.65,
          "en": "because I don't care in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.65,
          "end": 56.33,
          "en": "if it's an array full of numbers or strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.33,
          "end": 58.363,
          "en": "or of personal objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.23,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "Whatever it is, what I wanna do in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 64.803,
          "en": "is I wanna create a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 69.76,
          "en": "for example by using the spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.76,
          "end": 72.3,
          "en": "and copying the existing array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 75.28999999999999,
          "en": "that's a standard modern JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.28999999999999,
          "end": 77.093,
          "en": "also supported by TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.95,
          "end": 80.77,
          "en": "And then in front of that old array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.77,
          "end": 82.443,
          "en": "I wanna insert the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.32,
          "end": 88.623,
          "en": "And then I want to return this new array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.78,
          "end": 91.98,
          "en": "That could be a utility helper function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.98,
          "end": 94.16,
          "en": "which we create to have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.16,
          "end": 97.03,
          "en": "which we can easily call to add a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.03,
          "end": 100.08,
          "en": "in an array without changing the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.08,
          "end": 102.03999999999999,
          "en": "So the advantage of this function could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.03999999999999,
          "end": 104.57,
          "en": "that the original array never changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.57,
          "end": 107.033,
          "en": "but instead we're getting a brand new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.53,
          "end": 109.363,
          "en": "Now for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.363,
          "end": 111.7,
          "en": "I could of course have a demo array with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.7,
          "end": 113.93,
          "en": "let's say free values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.93,
          "end": 117.94,
          "en": "and then I get my updated array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.94,
          "end": 119.53999999999999,
          "en": "Where I call 'insertAtBeginning'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.52,
          "end": 122.56,
          "en": "and I pass in the demo array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.56,
          "end": 127.283,
          "en": "And then a value of minus one let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.12,
          "end": 130.8,
          "en": "With that, I know that the updated array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 134.94,
          "en": "will be this array with minus one inserted at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 139.94,
          "en": "So this will give me minus one, one, two, three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.06,
          "end": 143.2,
          "en": "And hence thereafter I might wanna do things with that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.2,
          "end": 146.32,
          "en": "which I can do with an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.32,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "But the problem is that updated array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 149.63,
          "en": "if I hover over it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.63,
          "end": 152.48,
          "en": "is inferred to be of type any array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.48,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "So an array full of any kind of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 158.47,
          "en": "TypeScript here doesn't pick up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.47,
          "end": 160.55,
          "en": "that it's an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.55,
          "end": 164.95,
          "en": "Why, because here I have any, as a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.95,
          "end": 168.2,
          "en": "And I can't say that I only wanna allow numbers here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.2,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "because what if I want to use this utility function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 173.703,
          "en": "with an array full of strings?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.74,
          "end": 177.17000000000002,
          "en": "So we need any, but at the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.35,
          "en": "that kind of removes all kind of TypeScript support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.35,
          "end": 184.18,
          "en": "we might be getting after calling this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.18,
          "end": 187.88,
          "en": "We're not getting any good TypeScript support for updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.88,
          "end": 190.55,
          "en": "array thereafter, because that is an inferred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.55,
          "end": 193.24,
          "en": "to be an array full of any kind of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.24,
          "end": 195.2,
          "en": "or any kind of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.2,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "And that's not useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 200.63,
          "en": "If I then for example, try to access the first element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.63,
          "end": 204.2,
          "en": "and called split here, which I could call on a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.2,
          "end": 206.03,
          "en": "I don't get an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.03,
          "end": 208.72,
          "en": "I would get a runtime error instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.72,
          "end": 211.34,
          "en": "because I can't call split on a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.34,
          "end": 214.84,
          "en": "But again, TypeScript doesn't know that the first value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.84,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "in updated array is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 220.36,
          "en": "We know it as a developer, but because of our type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.36,
          "end": 222.66,
          "en": "definitions here, which we need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 224.87,
          "en": "TypeScript doesn't know it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.87,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "And to work around such problems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 229.22,
          "en": "we have this feature of Generics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.22,
          "end": 232.51,
          "en": "and that's why I had does lengthy introduction here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.51,
          "end": 235.61,
          "en": "because it is important to understand why",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.61,
          "end": 237.32,
          "en": "this feature exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237.32,
          "end": 241.64,
          "en": "With this Generics feature, we can convert this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.64,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "to a Generic function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.56,
          "en": "For this we use a special syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.56,
          "end": 248.23,
          "en": "after the function name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.23,
          "end": 252.31,
          "en": "in front of the parameter list, we add angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.31,
          "end": 255.68,
          "en": "and that's now not a standard JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.68,
          "end": 258.07,
          "en": "but really only a feature we can use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.07,
          "end": 260.37,
          "en": "since we're using TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.37,
          "end": 265.04,
          "en": "And in here we can define a Generic type which will only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.04,
          "end": 267.88,
          "en": "be available inside of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 267.88,
          "end": 270.49,
          "en": "Typically that's called T for type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.49,
          "end": 273.763,
          "en": "but any identifier of your choices okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 275.23,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "Now you can use this type in your function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 280.03,
          "en": "including the parameter list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 280.03,
          "end": 284.12,
          "en": "And here I'm saying, I want to use this for my array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 284.12,
          "end": 288.553,
          "en": "So my array will be full of Ts and my value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 291.913,
          "en": "This should always be of type T.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 292.92,
          "end": 294.92,
          "en": "But how does this help us?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 294.92,
          "end": 298.19,
          "en": "Well like this set of codes it's just very cryptic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.19,
          "end": 302.81,
          "en": "but now when we call this function, now TypeScript actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 302.81,
          "end": 305.6,
          "en": "is able to understand that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 305.6,
          "end": 310.15,
          "en": "it should look at the concrete values of the arguments here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.15,
          "end": 313.07,
          "en": "And it understands that this is an array of numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 313.07,
          "end": 316.29,
          "en": "and this is just a number and they are free to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.29,
          "end": 319.91,
          "en": "that updated array will be an array of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.91,
          "end": 323.53,
          "en": "Because of this generic type feature, because we're telling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.53,
          "end": 328.53,
          "en": "TypeScript that the type here is actually not any type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.92,
          "end": 330.83,
          "en": "it's not any kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.83,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "Instead, we tell it that the type of this array and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 337.94,
          "en": "of this value should be the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.94,
          "end": 339.51,
          "en": "just that this is an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.51,
          "end": 342.88,
          "en": "but it's an array full of the same types of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 342.88,
          "end": 345.64,
          "en": "as this single value has it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 345.64,
          "end": 348.3,
          "en": "And that's an important piece of information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.3,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "Therefore, TypeScript is able to look at the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 353.67,
          "en": "of demo array, which it knows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.67,
          "end": 356.81,
          "en": "It knows that this is a, an array of numbers it's able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.81,
          "end": 360.14,
          "en": "to infer this, and it looks at this type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.14,
          "end": 363.53,
          "en": "And then it knows that logically, the array which gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.53,
          "end": 366.98,
          "en": "constructed here has to be of the same type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.98,
          "end": 368.19,
          "en": "as the input array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 368.19,
          "end": 370.04,
          "en": "It's able to infer this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 370.04,
          "end": 371.84,
          "en": "And hence, it's able to infer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.84,
          "end": 375.85,
          "en": "that what we get back here has to be an array of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 375.85,
          "end": 380.85,
          "en": "And if I would call, 'insertAtBeginning' here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.96,
          "end": 384.35,
          "en": "with an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384.35,
          "end": 388.103,
          "en": "Like this, and I then pass in a string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 388.96,
          "end": 391.06,
          "en": "and I have my string array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 391.06,
          "end": 394.13,
          "en": "TypeScript is also able to infer this correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 394.13,
          "end": 396.89,
          "en": "because again, it looks at this type and this type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 396.89,
          "end": 400.3,
          "en": "and it knows that the return type is of the same value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 400.3,
          "end": 403.46,
          "en": "as this type, as T input array, enhance it again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 403.46,
          "end": 405.2,
          "en": "infers this correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 405.2,
          "end": 408.48,
          "en": "And therefore for the updated array here where it knows",
